I am by no means an excellent player, although I don't suck.  Since
October 1st, I'm 5-for-11 on NAO.

some bits of advice to enhance one's survival:

1) Play slower.  All but one of my recent defeats were caused by
playing too fast.

2) When in doubt, save and come back later so you don't do something
dumb ... like press keys.

3) Engrave no more than 2-3 letters at a time with a hard gem (this
caused the "other" recent NAO death).

4) Be Paranoid.  Never forget, the RNG is actively trying to kill your
character at all times.

5) Watch your last game, try to figure out *where* you made your fatal
mistake.

6) Check everything twice, especially when there are/were foo-trices,
floating eyes, and (master) mind flayers nearby.

7) Remember, #twoweapon burns a move.  This could be critical during a
tense moment.

8) Have a plan.  A bad/unwise plan is better than plan 'b' (a.k.a.
"wing it").

9) Develop an "early-game" wishlist of 4-6 luxary items/intrinsics you
want to have.  Don't hesitate to blow a wish in a way that gets you
something off this list.

10) Never be too proud to wish for something "stupid".  I've "wasted"
wishes on blessed unicorn horns, many (non-artifact) athames, tins of
fire giant meat, oilskin sacks, unicorn/dragon corpses, and other
things that would cause some very experienced/skilled players to have
apoplectic fits.

11) If you have a non-cursed athame, don't hesitate to *SPAM* elbereth
from one end of the dungeon to the other.  "That's a grid bug, time to
e-word."  "Oh look, a fox, where's my athame?"

12) Every item in nethack has a positive use, even a scroll of amnesia.

13) There is no single correct solution or way to play the game.  Find
what works for you and what doesn't work for you ... and (most
importantly) stick to it.

